    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Data availability and identification evidence",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Device selection uses hostnames, not MAC addresses.** Devices without a known hostname display their current IP. The collector still uses MAC internally to keep device history when DHCP addresses change. OS classifications marked inferred come from DNS/Nmap clues; unknown ports or timed-out scans are **not** evidence that all ports are closed. CPU, memory, patch and filesystem graphs require Node Exporter and are unavailable for many phones, cameras and smart-home devices. DNS hints are evidence-qualified observations; continuous automated DNS investigation is not yet enabled."
      }
    },
